omx-plugins (0.17.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * round-trip: the losses each format cannot carry, counted over the 29
    plugins of 0.17.0 (the six faces, suboct and plosive added)
  * omx-delay: the release's declaration, which exposes the taps its
    generated header and descriptor carry
  * resource hints: the figures are xsd:integer, as omx-contract 3.6.0 ranges
    them (omx-contract#168); the untyped arm is now a figure written as a
    string
  * ci: the package builds drop the stale units sheet too, under CI only; the
    bridge carries its SPDX line
  * ci: the stale-sheet bridge also drops the manifest entry, and brings
    omx-panel 0.8.1
  * omx-delay holds omx-dsp 0.28.0's tap arguments; the floor is 0.28.0
  * ci: the package no longer ships param-units.json, and a job drops the
    stale copy the channel's omx-plugins-contract installs
  * generator: a chain's identity test spans no stretch either; omx-strip's
    test builds again
  * omx plugins: the six faces, suboct and plosive state their resource
    hints; every figure typed xsd:integer, regenerated
  * resource hints: the figures are xsd:integer, as omx-contract 3.6.0's
    vocabulary ranges them
  * tests: the upward compressor's ratio is a ratio control in the descriptor
    view
  * version 0.17.0: the delay's taps, the six faces, omx-suboct and
    omx-plosive, omx-dsp 0.28.0 and omx-contract 3.6.0, regenerated
  * omx plugins: the kernel-identity tests for the new faces and the delay's
    taps
  * omx plugins: the generated parameter headers, LV2 descriptions, MOD GUIs
    and presets for 0.28.0 and the new faces
  * docs: the catalogue, the parameter pages and the dependency table
  * omx plugins: factory presets for the six faces
  * packaging: the six faces; floors omx-dsp 0.28.0 and omx-contract 3.6.0
  * omx plugins: faces and bindings over omx-dsp 0.28.0 (the delay's taps,
    six new faces)
  * omx clipper, upward, glue, loudlevel, balancer and spring, and omx
    delay's taps: declarations and descriptors, omx-dsp 0.28.0 sources
  * generator: stretch, liveStretch and sabotageStep for kernels that adapt
    over seconds; the live test and param-units check read the installed
    header
  * release workflow: the rpm build from the shared workflows at v1.1.1,
    whose build job may run 120 minutes
  * omx suboct and omx plosive: in the README's catalogue and the parameter
    pages
  * omx suboct and omx plosive: factory presets
  * omx suboct and omx plosive: the kernel-identity tests
  * packaging: omx suboct and omx plosive in omx-plugins-clap and
    omx-plugins-lv2
  * omx suboct and omx plosive: CLAP and LV2 faces in plain C over omx-dsp's
    kernels
  * omx suboct and omx plosive: the generated parameter headers and LV2
    descriptions
  * omx suboct and omx plosive: their declarations, parameters by reference
    to the kernels
  * BUILDING: resolve the merge marks left in the dependency table; omx-dsp
    >= 0.27.0
  * descriptors: the schema floor is 3.1.0, the release that added dB/oct
    (omx-comp's key tilt)
  * param-contract: the unit codes come from omx-contract 3.6.0
    (OMX_PARAM_CONTRACT_UNITS, omx_param_units.h)
  * version 0.16.1: the thread-pool test instrument (#284), regenerated
  * ci: the test, selftest, RPM and DEB jobs may run 120 minutes
  * debian/control: wrap the test package's description at 80 columns
  * version 0.16.1
  * omx-test-pool-voice: a test instrument that renders its voices as
    clap.thread-pool tasks
  * dyneq's band centres and the multiband's crossovers are authored log, the
    compressor's key filters stay stepped from 0 (#276)
  * round trip: the clap scale losses of 21 plugins agree with main's log
    authoring (#179)
  * comp-key.c: the reference compressor takes omx-dsp 0.27.0's release mode
    at its default (#179)
  * The descriptor reader weighs a travel's minimum when it names an integer
    frequency's scale (#276)
  * Build against omx-dsp 0.27.0: the floor is 0.27.0 and the compressor's
    release mode is held at fixed
  * The reverb's cuts pin no logarithmic; the build floor is plugin-hostd
    0.15.2 (#276)
  * round trip: the named losses of 21 plugins, the dyneq and multiband's
    among them (#179)
  * Regenerate the merged plugins against main: omx-dyneq and omx-multiband
    at 0.16.0, the parameter reference (#179)
  * comp-key.c: its header line names the file with a colon (#179)
  * tests: the pinned counts of this release, 21 described plugins: the
    designations, the ratio controls and the round trip's named losses (#179)
  * omx-multiband: the multiband compressor, two to five bands, from omx-dsp
    0.26.0's mbcomp kernel file (FX-3, #179)
  * omx-dyneq: the six-band dynamic EQ, from omx-dsp 0.26.0's dyneq kernel
    file (FX-1, #179)
  * docs: the designations and the round trip's named losses of 21 described
    plugins, the dB/oct unit among them (#179)
  * omx-comp: key listen is a monitor, its pins leave the custom unit URNs
    the pin pattern refuses, compKey joins the meter fixture (#179)
  * panel-layout: dB/oct is a descriptor unit, omx-contract 3.1.0's, the
    compressor's key tilt (#179)
  * meter-level digests the levels a face measures, two channels; a level the
    kernel reads is held with the others, within a tolerance (#179)
  * A defaultRef may index a list: MBC_CROSSOVER_DEFAULTS_3.0 (#179)
  * clap-probe live tries each other toggle on alone with the choices at
    their far values, then each pair of other travels at their ends (#179)
  * A chain's element over a keyable face runs run_keyed with no key, so its
    key filter, tilt and link act on its own legs (#179)
  * The sabotage step of an integer travel is its 1 % in whole steps, of a
    time travel 5 %: a step a float pole can see (#179)
  * The identity plan holds a declaration's monitors at their default where
    the others move, and its engaged values in the release and choice
    sections (#179)
  * The wizard writes a new plugin described: its descriptor rendered from
    the settled declaration, the declaration reduced to its extras (#179)
  * docs: the sabotage arm's step, an integer travel's share in whole steps
    and 5 % of a time travel (#179)
  * docs: a declaration's engaged values hold a band driven in the identity
    plan's release and choice sections (#179)
  * docs: a monitor parameter, one that replaces the output while on, is held
    at its default where the identity plan moves or steps the others (#179)
  * docs: the wizard writes a new plugin described, its descriptor and its
    declaration's extras (#179)
  * defaultBand names a contract count: a band's centre by the EQ default
    rule in a bank of DYNEQ_BANDS (#179)
  * docs: a band's centre with no declared default comes up by the EQ default
    rule at a contract count, defaultBand's count (#179)
  * omx-comp takes its key: a sidechain port, the KEY and DUCK sections, nine
    controls from comp.json and the compKey meter (FX-2, #179)
  * clap-probe live tries each other travel at either end with the rest at
    their defaults: a ducker heard only past its depth (#179)
  * BUILDING: omx-dsp >= 0.26.0, the dynamic EQ, the multiband's controls and
    the compressor's key; omx-panel >= 0.2.5 (#179)
  * The wizard drafts a band per count a control declares where the face's
    extent is its own macro; dyneq drafts as eq, mbcomp as dynamics (#179)
  * A meter reads the kernel through the face: read names a float reading of
    the instance, and a level the kernel reads is one channel (#179)
  * A plugin declares fixed controls as a chain element does: no parameter,
    passed at their value to the face and the reference (#179)
  * The face reader knows a keyable face: run_keyed beside an unkeyed run,
    the plugin keyed when it names a sidechain (#179)
  * docs: a keyable face's run_keyed, a plugin's fixed controls, a meter read
    through the face and the per-band count a control declares (#179)
  * omx-geq declares the fader for its 31 bands (#231)
  * The deesser, drive and phaser frequencies are authored log; a Hz travel
    from 0 is not logarithmic (#276)
  * An integer frequency is authored log, as its LV2 face states it (#276)
  * round trip: the toggle entry goes with plugin-hostd 0.15.1, the scale
    entry names its class (#276)
  * DEB builds: python3 in the CI DEB job, and version reads without make's
    directory lines (#278)
  * Say decided and decision in the comments, as the maintainers write it
  * debian: serdi is a build dependency of the checks
  * Regenerate against omx-panel 0.7.1: MOD GUI text in Inter, the phaser's
    depth published (#232)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 04:44:59 +0000
